{# PM·RISK — TWO STANDING RISKS, and both are properties of shipped code rather
   than of anybody's configuration. Neither has a button, because neither has a
   done that a button could reach. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/positions/_bits.html.twig' as pm %}

<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Standing risks<span class="src">&middot; nothing here is dismissible</span></span>
    <div class="tm-att">
        {% if soleSuperAdmin %}
            <div class="tm-attrow r standing">
                {{ pm.icon_warn() }}
                <div class="at">
                    <b>One Super Admin, and no recovery path</b>
                    <p>The model has no break-glass account, no second owner flag and no audit trail. If that one
                    account is lost the installation is administered from a database client or not at all. The
                    code refuses to let it be demoted or deactivated, which stops the accident and does not fix
                    the exposure &mdash; grant the tier to a successor.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if orphans is not empty %}
            <div class="tm-attrow w standing">
                {{ pm.icon_warn() }}
                <div class="at">
                    <b>{{ orphans|length }} grant{{ orphans|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} no installed module provides</b>
                    <p>A bundle that declared {% for value in orphans|keys %}<span class="perm">{{ value }}</span>{% endfor %}
                    has been removed, and positions still hold the values. They resolve to nothing today and would
                    start working again if the module came back &mdash; which is why they were pruned rather than
                    purged. Untick one on its position to take it away for good.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if not soleSuperAdmin and orphans is empty %}
            <div class="tm-settled">
                {{ pm.icon_info() }}
                <span>Neither standing risk applies: more than one Super Admin can sign in, and every grant on
                every position is provided by something installed.</span>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
